"Artonans are aliens, nicknamed space wizards, from the home planet Artona."
"They brought the System to Earth and to many other planets."
"They give powers, arcane knowledge and technology in return for help when they call."
"Humans hold them fair: they offer rewards equal to the task given."
"Few Artonans live on Earth."
"Their planetary flags are multicolored streamers."
"Their writing is logographic and takes brutal memorization."
"Their history marks when life on Artona began to understand the magic of the planes."
"It is rude to wear shoes or socks before an Artonan who is teaching you."
"They sometimes tell Earth when a hero dies on a quest, but mostly do not."
"Some humans form Artonan cults."
"Gorgon says Artonans prefer not to help Earth along, giving meager or misleading instructions."
"Artonans think of other peoples as lower species."
"Artonan law holds that all Avowed are justly rewarded for any service rendered."
"Artonans of the highest ranks all deal with true demons."
"Artonans greatly value beauty."
"Calling sentient beings by animal names is normally unacceptable to Artonans."
"Helpful children and useful junior staff are fondly called Little Ryeh-b'ts."
"Artonan children send gifts and messages by pet Ryeh-b't."
"Artonan weddings sometimes join three brides and grooms at once."
"Artonans carry titles such as Honorable, as in the biologist Honorable Ty-krol."
"About twenty percent of Artonans are the magic-using wizard class that rules."
"The other eighty percent are second class and cannot hold office or vote."
"Wizard garb is harem pants, a tight turtleneck and a loose wide-sleeved overcoat."
"Artonans are a few inches shorter than humans on average."
"Artonans like indoor heat just shy of ninety degrees Fahrenheit."
"Artonans open conversations by giving their names."
"Artonan bartenders share the first drink with each patron."
"Artonans see Avowed variously as children, beasts of burden, holy gifts or existential threats."
"Wizard crimes can be punished by sentences such as teaching, and by loss of System privileges."
"Artonan law cannot blame children or Ryeh-b'ts for crimes a wizard tricked them into."
"Wevvi, spiced fruit juice tasting like eggnog served near boiling, is a hospitality drink."
"Artonan eyes can point different ways and process two images at once."
"Artonans are good multitaskers; humans are poor ones by comparison."
"Many Artonans have magitech implants, such as gold rings around the irises."
"Artonan wizards are highly educated, proud, and feel superior to other species."
"Artonan parties are deliberately messy, with brim-full drinks, hookahs and heavy drinking."
"Artonan children treat costumed Avowed like theme-park characters."
"Artonans are the most numerous highly intelligent species known."
"Artonans constantly try to mitigate chaos."
"Artonans drink hot drinks rather than chilled ones in winter."
"Artonans can run two separate conscious thoughts at once, one per eye."
"Artonans age a little more slowly than humans."
"Artonans hold kind lies to children an act of love; withholding one hurts."
"Artonan children's shows end with a teacher explaining the moral; every fifth one is dark."
"Artonans go barefoot for lessons and kneel on learning cushions."
"The Artonan word for me expresses one's place in relation to everything in the universe."
"Humans and Artonans share most foods, but shellfish on the Triplanets is a very bad idea."
"Polite requests for assistance are the proper way to earn a passing wizard's help."
"Ceremonial blood is not mixed with other ingredients, and ancient prophets heard voices."
